  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.1-preview.30\n- Updated to depend on FireForNet.Firebase.Firestore 1.0.1-preview.30, which fixes offline ServerAndCache reads so they fall back to the cache, maps gRPC call-creation failures to FirestoreErrorCode.Unavailable, makes cached timestamp filters match server-cached Timestamp values at Firestore native precision, and fixes Timestamp.FromDateTime/FromDateTimeOffset throwing for pre-1970 instants. Persisted field indexes from earlier previews are rebuilt automatically on open; no manual migration is required. BREAKING: the parameterless WithConverter<TModel>() is removed; use Collection<T>()/Document<T>() for JSON auto-conversion or WithConverter with a converter/delegates. Custom model conversion now runs through internal document codecs on native references and queries (the Converted* wrapper hierarchy is retired), and IDocumentSnapshot<T>.TryGet(field, out value) distinguishes an absent field from a stored null.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.29\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.29 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.28\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.28 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.27\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.27 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.26\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.26 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.25\n- Fixes Mac Catalyst. The package now ships a net10.0-maccatalyst asset and delegates to Firestore.Apple on that head. Previously a net10.0-maccatalyst consumer resolved the plain net10.0 browser asset, so UseUno() threw UnoFirestoreException at startup.\n- Mac Catalyst defines MACCATALYST (and __IOS__), not IOS. The per-head dispatch is now IOS || MACCATALYST in both the using block and the registration branch; fixing only the asset or only the symbol leaves the failure in place.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.24\n- Adds the Uno Platform integration for Cloud Firestore. UseUno() delegates to the platform package that matches the Uno head the application is running on.\n- The package references no Uno package and stays framework-independent, exactly as the .Maui packages reference no MAUI package. The head is detected at runtime, so the browser and Skia-desktop heads share the plain net10.0 asset.\n- Fails fast with UnoFirestoreException on the Skia desktop head, including Linux, because FireForNet ships no desktop integration packages.",
